+---
+id: task-002-equipment-availability-query
+type: task
+title: "Equipment availability query"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Equipment availability query
+
+Request: the desk needs to see at a glance what can still be rented. Add `availability(query)` to the
+rental service, where `query` is `{ start, end, kind }` and `kind` is optional. It returns the ids of the
+equipment of that kind, or of any kind when none is given, that is free for the whole period, sorted.
+
+## Scope
+
+- `RentalService` gains `availability({ start, end, kind? }): string[]`.
+  - `start` and `end` are validated as `quote` and `book` validate their period: UTC ISO-8601 timestamps
+    at midnight UTC, `end` after `start`.
+  - `kind` is optional. When given it must be `'board'` or `'sail'`; any other value throws.
+  - The result holds the ids of the matching equipment that has no booking overlapping `[start, end)`,
+    sorted in ascending code-unit order.
+- Export the `AvailabilityQuery` type from `src/index.ts`.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- With no `kind`, every item (board or sail) that is free for the whole period is listed.
+- With a `kind`, only items of that kind are listed.
+- An item booked for a period overlapping `[start, end)` is left out; a back-to-back booking does not
+  overlap, so the item is listed.
+- An item with no bookings is listed.
+- The result is sorted, so it is deterministic regardless of insertion order.
+- No equipment, or none free, gives an empty array.
+- An unknown `kind` throws, and an invalid period throws, as `quote` and `book` do.
+- `availability` does not reserve anything: a later `book` for a listed period still succeeds.
+
+## Rules applied
+
+1. Money is an integer number of euro cents (not involved here).
+2. Times are in UTC, written as ISO-8601 strings.
+3. A booking covers whole days only.
+4. Periods are half-open: `[start, end)`.
+5. The same item cannot be booked twice for overlapping periods.
+
+## Traceability
+
+Request -> this task -> acceptance above -> tests in `src/rental.test.ts`. It extends the rules of
+`task-001-rental-module-basics`.
